>> Is there anything that's particularly advisable to wipe out at turn
>> 1, if you're lucky enough to start with the scroll? I've seen hints

> Mimics, water moccasins, gelatinous cubes.

Mimics are easy to avoid, water moccasins aren't an issue if you don't
go recklessly quaffing, and gelatinous cubes are a valuable source of
intrinsics that move very slowly and do little damage.  

> ants, leprechauns (a pain when they take your 2000 gold pieces you
> just stole from that vault), water nymphs, rust monsters(I lost a +5
> elven dagger to rust monsters today). 

Ants are a viable target, but better to keep the scroll for an
emergency.  Leprechauns do little damage and you can drop your gold
before you fight them.  Nymphs start sleeping, so don't wake them.  Rust
monsters do zero damage.

> For more advanced game I'd
> genocide mind flayers, master mind flayers, green slimes, vampire
> lords, arch-liches, electric eels and so on.

Mind flayers are a pain, but respect engravings.  Green slimes are
practically stationary.  Vampire lords do trivial damage and have a
miniscule chance of draining if you have MC=3.  Arch-liches are a good
choice.  Eels can be killed with telepathy and a pile of rocks. 

In the early game, best to just carry the scroll until it's an
emergency.

